// Temperate forest mammals (Appendix B tier 1), Palearctic and Nearctic. Masses, speeds,
// densities and life histories are rounded values for wild adults from general mammal
// references (Macdonald's Encyclopedia of Mammals, the Handbook of the Mammals of the World,
// species accounts); daily food is dry matter for herbivores and fresh meat for carnivores.
// Yields are fractions of the live mass; the mass range is of both sexes, `dimorphism` how much
// heavier a grown male is (V2-7 (h)). Life history (V2-7): first breeding age, the oldest
// age commonly reached, litter, births a year, the usual birth day (day of the year, north),
// survival from causes the simulation does not model (disease, accident, old age), newborn mass.
